#: ../../source/design.rst:87
msgid "Assemblies"
msgstr "Ensamblajes"

#: ../../source/design.rst:89
msgid ""
"Assemblies are parametrized instructions on how to put parts and other "
"assemblies together."
msgstr ""
"Los ensamblajes son instrucciones parametrizadas sobre cómo unir piezas y"
" otros ensamblajes."

#: ../../source/design.rst:92
msgid ""
"PartCAD is expected to have an ever-growing list of ways to define "
"assemblies using existing parts. However, at the moment, only one way is "
"supported. It is called ASSY: assembly YAML. The idea behind ASSY is to "
"create a simplistic way to enumerate parts, define their parameters and "
"define how parts connect."
msgstr ""
"Se espera que PartCAD tenga una lista en constante crecimiento de formas "
"de definir ensamblajes usando piezas existentes. Sin embargo, por el "
"momento solo se admite una forma. Se llama ASSY: assembly YAML. La idea "
"detrás de ASSY es crear una forma simplificada de enumerar piezas, "
"definir sus parámetros y definir cómo se conectan las piezas."

#: ../../source/design.rst:100
msgid "Scenes"
msgstr "Escenas"

#: ../../source/design.rst:102
msgid ""
"PartCAD does not yet implement scenes. But the idea is to be able to "
"reproduce the same features as worlds in Gazebo to the extent that "
"PartCAD scenes can be exported to and simulated in Gazebo, but without "
"using XML while creating the scene."
msgstr ""
"PartCAD todavía no implementa escenas. Pero la idea es poder reproducir "
"las mismas características que los mundos (\"worlds\") en Gazebo, de modo"
" que las escenas de PartCAD se puedan exportar y simular en Gazebo, pero "
"sin usar XML al crear la escena."

#: ../../source/design.rst:108
msgid "Monorepos"
msgstr "Monorepos"

#: ../../source/design.rst:110
msgid ""
"When PartCAD is initialized, the current folder and its ``partcad.yaml`` "
"become the `current` package, but not the `root` package. The root "
"package is discovered by traversing the parent directories for as long as"
" there is another ``partcad.yaml`` found there."
msgstr ""
"Cuando se inicializa PartCAD, la carpeta actual y su ``partcad.yaml`` se "
"convierten en el paquete `current`, pero no en el paquete `root`. El "
"paquete raíz se descubre recorriendo los directorios padre mientras se "
"siga encontrando otro ``partcad.yaml`` en ellos."

#: ../../source/design.rst:115
msgid ""
"This allows to run PartCAD tools from any sub-directory in a monorepo "
"project while maintaining the same meaning of relative and absolute "
"paths."
msgstr ""
"Esto permite ejecutar las herramientas de PartCAD desde cualquier "
"subdirectorio de un proyecto monorepo manteniendo el mismo significado de"
" las rutas relativas y absolutas."

#: ../../source/design.rst:119
msgid "Paths"
msgstr "Rutas"

#: ../../source/design.rst:121
msgid ""
"PartCAD uses package paths to identify packages and parts declared in "
"them."
msgstr ""
"PartCAD usa rutas de paquete para identificar los paquetes y las piezas "
"declaradas en ellos."

#: ../../source/design.rst:123
msgid ""
"The current package has the path ``\"\"`` or ``\".\"``. The root package "
"has the path ``\"//\"``. For any package ``\"<package-path>\"``, each "
"sub-directory containing ``partcad.yaml`` and each ``import``-ed "
"dependency becomes ``\"<package-path>/<sub-package>\"``."
msgstr ""
"El paquete actual tiene la ruta ``\"\"`` o ``\".\"``. El paquete raíz "
"tiene la ruta ``\"//\"``. Para cualquier paquete ``\"<package-path>\"``, "
"cada subdirectorio que contenga ``partcad.yaml`` y cada dependencia "
"``import``-ada se convierte en ``\"<package-path>/<sub-package>\"``."

#: ../../source/design.rst:130
msgid "Absolute vs relative"
msgstr "Absoluta frente a relativa"

#: ../../source/design.rst:132
msgid ""
"The absolute package path is the path from the root package to the "
"package. If the path starts with ``\"//\"`` then it is an absolute path."
msgstr ""
"La ruta de paquete absoluta es la ruta desde el paquete raíz hasta el "
"paquete. Si la ruta comienza con ``\"//\"``, entonces es una ruta "
"absoluta."

#: ../../source/design.rst:135
msgid ""
"The relative package path is the path from the current package to the "
"package. If the path does not start with ``\"//\"`` then it is a relative"
" path. Sometimes it might help to disambiguate the relative path by "
"prepending ``\"./\"``."
msgstr ""
"La ruta de paquete relativa es la ruta desde el paquete actual hasta el "
"paquete. Si la ruta no comienza con ``\"//\"``, entonces es una ruta "
"relativa. A veces puede ayudar a desambiguar la ruta relativa anteponer "
"``\"./\"``."

#: ../../source/design.rst:140
msgid "Multiple packages"
msgstr "Múltiples paquetes"

#: ../../source/design.rst:142
msgid ""
"Some PartCAD commands and interfaces allow referencing multiple packages "
"at once. ``\"<package-path>/\\*\"`` is a reference to all sub-packages in"
" ``\"<package-path>\"``."
msgstr ""
"Algunos comandos e interfaces de PartCAD permiten hacer referencia a "
"múltiples paquetes a la vez. ``\"<package-path>/\\*\"`` es una referencia"
" a todos los subpaquetes en ``\"<package-path>\"``."

#: ../../source/design.rst:145
msgid ""
"``\"<package-path>/...\"`` is a reference to ``\"<package-path>\"`` and "
"to all of its sub-packages."
msgstr ""
"``\"<package-path>/...\"`` es una referencia a ``\"<package-path>\"`` y a"
" todos sus subpaquetes."

#: ../../source/design.rst:149
msgid "Object IDs"
msgstr "IDs de objeto"

#: ../../source/design.rst:151
msgid ""
"PartCAD packages contain objects of different types: *sketches*, *parts*,"
" *assemblies*, *scenes*, *interfaces*, *providers* and so on. All of them"
" need to get referenced."
msgstr ""
"Los paquetes de PartCAD contienen objetos de diferentes tipos: "
"*sketches*, *parts*, *assemblies*, *scenes*, *interfaces*, *providers*, "
"etc. Todos ellos deben ser referenciados."

#: ../../source/design.rst:156
msgid "Single object"
msgstr "Objeto único"

#: ../../source/design.rst:158
msgid ""
"Each object has a unique name within the package (across all object "
"types). The object can be globally identified using ``\"<package-path"
">:<object-name>\"``."
msgstr ""
"Cada objeto tiene un nombre único dentro del paquete (en todos los tipos "
"de objeto). El objeto se puede identificar globalmente usando "
"``\"<package-path>:<object-name>\"``."

#: ../../source/design.rst:161
msgid ""
"An attempt to reference an object using the object-name alone is "
"considered a reference to the object in the current package."
msgstr ""
"Un intento de hacer referencia a un objeto usando solo el nombre del "
"objeto se considera una referencia al objeto en el paquete actual."

#: ../../source/design.rst:165
msgid "Multiple objects"
msgstr "Múltiples objetos"

#: ../../source/design.rst:167
msgid ""
"Some PartCAD commands and interfaces allow referencing multiple objects "
"at once. ``\"<single-or-multiple-package-path>/:\\*\"`` is a reference to"
" all objects in ``\"<single-or-multiple-package-path>\"``."
msgstr ""
"Algunos comandos e interfaces de PartCAD permiten hacer referencia a "
"múltiples objetos a la vez. ``\"<single-or-multiple-package-"
"path>/:\\*\"`` es una referencia a todos los objetos en ``\"<single-or-"
"multiple-package-path>\"``."

#: ../../source/design.rst:173
msgid "Parametrized objects"
msgstr "Objetos parametrizados"

#: ../../source/design.rst:175
msgid ""
"Some objects (such as *sketches*, *parts*, *assemblies*, *interfaces* and"
" *providers*) may have parameters specified within the object ID to "
"identify an instantiation of the object with the given parameters: "
"``\"<package-path>:<object-name>;param1=value1,param2=value2\"``."
msgstr ""
"Algunos objetos (como *sketches*, *parts*, *assemblies*, *interfaces* y "
"*providers*) pueden tener parámetros especificados dentro del ID del "
"objeto para identificar una instanciación del objeto con los parámetros "
"dados: ``\"<package-path>:<object-name>;param1=value1,param2=value2\"``."

#: ../../source/design.rst:192
msgid "Objects in a cart"
msgstr "Objetos en un carrito"

#: ../../source/design.rst:194
msgid ""
"Whenever an object (a *part* or an *assembly*) is used for manufacturing "
"or ordering from a store, the object ID may optionally contain the "
"quantity: ``\"<package-path>:<object-"
"name>;param1=value1,param2=value2#<quantity>\"``."
msgstr ""
"Cuando un objeto (una *part* o un *assembly*) se usa para fabricación o "
"para hacer un pedido en una tienda, el ID del objeto puede contener "
"opcionalmente la cantidad: ``\"<package-path>:<object-"
"name>;param1=value1,param2=value2#<quantity>\"``."

#: ../../source/design.rst:207
msgid "The public repository"
msgstr "El repositorio público"

#: ../../source/design.rst:209
msgid ""
"The public PartCAD repository is created and maintained by the community "
"based on the PartCAD standards and conventions. It is hosted on `GitHub "
"<https://github.com/partcad/partcad-index>`_."
msgstr ""
"El repositorio público de PartCAD es creado y mantenido por la comunidad "
"con base en los estándares y convenciones de PartCAD. Está alojado en "
"`GitHub <https://github.com/partcad/partcad-index>`_."

#: ../../source/design.rst:213
msgid ""
"The top levels of the package hierarchy are expected to be maintained by "
"the PartCAD community. Lower levels of the hierarchy are expected to be "
"maintained by vendors and other communities. PartCAD community does not "
"aim to achieve the uniqueness of parts and assemblies. Moreover, everyone"
" is invited to provide their alternative models as long as they provide a"
" different level of model quality or different level of package quality "
"management processes, and as long the package data properly reflects the "
"quality that the maintainer provides and commits to maintain. This way "
"PartCAD users have a choice of which model to use based on their specific"
" needs."
msgstr ""
"Se espera que los niveles superiores de la jerarquía de paquetes sean "
"mantenidos por la comunidad de PartCAD. Se espera que los niveles "
"inferiores de la jerarquía sean mantenidos por proveedores y otras "
"comunidades. La comunidad de PartCAD no pretende lograr la unicidad de "
"piezas y ensamblajes. Es más, se invita a todos a proporcionar sus "
"modelos alternativos siempre que ofrezcan un nivel diferente de calidad "
"de modelo o un nivel diferente de procesos de gestión de calidad del "
"paquete, y siempre que los datos del paquete reflejen adecuadamente la "
"calidad que el mantenedor proporciona y se compromete a mantener. De esta"
" manera, los usuarios de PartCAD tienen la posibilidad de elegir qué "
"modelo usar según sus necesidades específicas."

#: ../../source/design.rst:226
msgid "Tools"
msgstr "Herramientas"

#: ../../source/design.rst:228
msgid ""
"PartCAD tools can operate with public and private repositories for as "
"long as they are maintained following the PartCAD standards and "
"conventions."
msgstr ""
"Las herramientas de PartCAD pueden operar con repositorios públicos y "
"privados siempre que se mantengan siguiendo los estándares y convenciones"
" de PartCAD."

#: ../../source/design.rst:232
msgid "Command line tools"
msgstr "Herramientas de línea de comandos"

#: ../../source/design.rst:234
msgid ""
"PartCAD CLI tools get installed using the PyPI module ``partcad-cli``. "
"The main tool is called ``pc``. The CLI tools are supposed to provide the"
" complete set of PartCAD features."
msgstr ""
"Las herramientas de la CLI de PartCAD se instalan usando el módulo de "
"PyPI ``partcad-cli``. La herramienta principal se llama ``pc``. Se espera"
" que las herramientas de la CLI proporcionen el conjunto completo de "
"funcionalidades de PartCAD."

#: ../../source/design.rst:239
msgid "Visual Studio Code extension"
msgstr "Extensión de Visual Studio Code"

#: ../../source/design.rst:241
msgid "PartCAD extension for ``vscode`` is designed to be the primary tool."
msgstr ""
"La extensión de PartCAD para ``vscode`` está diseñada para ser la "
"herramienta principal."

#: ../../source/design.rst:246
msgid "Libraries and frameworks"
msgstr "Bibliotecas y marcos de trabajo"

#: ../../source/design.rst:249
msgid "Python"
msgstr "Python"

#: ../../source/design.rst:251
msgid ""
"The `partcad` Python module is the first PartCAD library. Its development"
" is prioritized due to the popularity and the value proposition of such "
"Python frameworks such as CadQuery and build123d."
msgstr ""
"El módulo Python `partcad` es la primera biblioteca de PartCAD. Su "
"desarrollo tiene prioridad debido a la popularidad y la propuesta de "
"valor de marcos de trabajo de Python como CadQuery y build123d."

#: ../../source/design.rst:256
msgid "Other languages"
msgstr "Otros lenguajes"

#: ../../source/design.rst:258
msgid ""
"PartCAD does not aim to stop at supporting Python. Native libraries in "
"other languages are planned and all contributors wishing to join the "
"project are welcome."
msgstr ""
"PartCAD no pretende limitarse a admitir Python. Se planean bibliotecas "
"nativas en otros lenguajes, y todos los colaboradores que deseen unirse "
"al proyecto son bienvenidos."
